  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Weave\n\nWarp and weft threads interlace on a gently warped grid while a slow sheen of light travels across the cloth, drawn in WebGL. An accent color can run through the threads.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 5 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- Tactile, crafted, made-of textures: fabric, mesh, or substrate metaphors.\n- A scene wants a slow sheen of light traveling across a textured surface.\n- The brand voice is handcrafted or material rather than digital and smooth.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You want a smooth gradient field: use shader-mesh-gradient.\n- You want organic noise instead of a woven structure: use shader-neuro-noise.\n\nVariables:\n- speed (number, 0-4): Speed, default 1\n- colors (string): Colors, default \"#12121a, #22223a, #3a3a5c, #c8c8d0\"\n- accent (color): Accent, default \"#6733FF\"\n- accent_amount (number, 0-1): Accent amount, default 0\n- scale (number, 6-60): Thread density, default 22\n- warp (number, 0-0.15): Warp, default 0.03\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Shader Weave\n\n  A woven substrate of warp and weft threads crossing on a domain-warped grid.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/shader-weave/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"shader-weave\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"How fast it moves. 0 holds still.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05},\n    {\"id\": \"colors\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Colors\", \"description\": \"Four colors, comma separated: fabric shadow, fabric mid, fabric warm, thread highlight.\", \"default\": \"#12121a, #22223a, #3a3a5c, #c8c8d0\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Accent\", \"description\": \"Tint carried by the threads (see Accent amount).\", \"default\": \"#6733FF\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent_amount\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Accent amount\", \"description\": \"How much of the accent shows, 0 to 1. The original animates it from the host timeline.\", \"default\": 0, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.01},\n    {\"id\": \"scale\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Thread density\", \"description\": \"Threads across the frame height.\", \"default\": 22, \"min\": 6, \"max\": 60, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"warp\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Warp\", \"description\": \"How hand-woven the threads bend, as a fraction of the frame.\", \"default\": 0.03, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 0.15, \"step\": 0.005},\n    {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the shader is drawn at, then scaled up. Lower renders faster; raise it when fine detail looks soft.\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Shader Weave</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: var(--swv-fallback, #0a0a12);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .swv-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n\n        .swv-canvas {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n        }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"shader-weave\" data-duration=\"5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"swv-clip\" class=\"swv-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"swv-canvas\" class=\"swv-canvas\"></canvas>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"swv-canvas\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, allowed, fallback) {\n              return allowed.indexOf(value) >= 0 ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function parseColor(s) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6}|[0-9a-f]{8})$/i.exec(String(s).trim());\n              if (!m) return null;\n              var h = m[1];\n              if (h.length === 3) h = h[0] + h[0] + h[1] + h[1] + h[2] + h[2];\n              var a = h.length === 8 ? parseInt(h.slice(6, 8), 16) / 255 : 1;\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) / 255, a];\n            }\n            function colorList(value, fallback, max) {\n              var list = String(typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback)\n                .split(\",\").map(parseColor).filter(Boolean).slice(0, max);\n              return list.length ? list : fallback.split(\",\").map(parseColor).slice(0, max);\n            }\n            function color(value, fallback) {\n              return parseColor(value) || parseColor(fallback);\n            }\n            function css(c) {\n              return \"rgba(\" + Math.round(c[0] * 255) + \",\" + Math.round(c[1] * 255) + \",\" + Math.round(c[2] * 255) + \",\" + c[3] + \")\";\n            }\n            function mulberry32(seed) {\n              return function () {\n                seed = (seed + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\n                var t = Math.imul(seed ^ (seed >>> 15), 1 | seed);\n                t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            function colorArray(list, max) {\n              var flat = new Float32Array(max * 4);\n              list.forEach(function (c, i) { flat.set(c, i * 4); });\n              return flat;\n            }\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0, 4);\n            var colors = colorList(vars.colors, \"#12121a, #22223a, #3a3a5c, #c8c8d0\", 4);\n            var accent = color(vars.accent, \"#6733FF\");\n            var accentAmount = num(vars.accent_amount, 0, 0, 1);\n            var scale = num(vars.scale, 22, 6, 60);\n            var warp = num(vars.warp, 0.03, 0, 0.15);\n            var resolution = num(vars.resolution, 0.75, 0.25, 1);\n            while (colors.length < 4) colors.push(colors[colors.length - 1]);\n\n            // Without WebGL the block still shows its palette as a plain gradient.\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--swv-fallback\", \"linear-gradient(160deg, \" + [colors[0], colors[2], colors[0]].map(css).join(\", \") + \")\");\n\n            var VERTEX = [\n              \"attribute vec2 a_pos;\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  gl_Position = vec4(a_pos, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n\n            var FRAGMENT = [\n              \"precision highp float;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"uniform vec2 u_res;\",\n              \"uniform float u_time;\",\n              \"uniform float u_scale;\",\n              \"uniform float u_warp;\",\n              \"uniform vec3 u_c0;\",\n              \"uniform vec3 u_c1;\",\n              \"uniform vec3 u_c2;\",\n              \"uniform vec3 u_c3;\",\n              \"uniform vec3 u_accent;\",\n              \"uniform float u_accentAmt;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"float hash(vec2 p) {\",\n              \"  return fract(sin(dot(p, vec2(127.1, 311.7))) * 43758.5453123);\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"float noise(vec2 p) {\",\n              \"  vec2 i = floor(p);\",\n              \"  vec2 f = fract(p);\",\n              \"  vec2 u = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f);\",\n              \"  return mix(\",\n              \"    mix(hash(i), hash(i + vec2(1.0, 0.0)), u.x),\",\n              \"    mix(hash(i + vec2(0.0, 1.0)), hash(i + vec2(1.0, 1.0)), u.x),\",\n              \"    u.y\",\n              \"  );\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"float fbm(vec2 p) {\",\n              \"  float v = 0.0;\",\n              \"  float a = 0.5;\",\n              \"  for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\",\n              \"    v += a * noise(p);\",\n              \"    p *= 2.03;\",\n              \"    a *= 0.5;\",\n              \"  }\",\n              \"  return v;\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"// A thin ridge line at every integer of x \\u2014 the profile of one thread.\",\n              \"float thread(float x, float sharp) {\",\n              \"  float f = fract(x);\",\n              \"  float d = min(f, 1.0 - f);\",\n              \"  return smoothstep(sharp, 0.0, d);\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  vec2 uv = gl_FragCoord.xy / u_res;\",\n              \"  float aspect = u_res.x / u_res.y;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  // Domain warp \\u2014 bend the weave so it reads hand-made, not a CSS grid. The\",\n              \"  // warp field drifts very slowly; the grid lattice itself stays put.\",\n              \"  vec2 q = uv + u_warp * vec2(\",\n              \"    fbm(uv * 3.0 + vec2(u_time * 0.03, 0.0)) - 0.5,\",\n              \"    fbm(uv * 3.0 + vec2(7.3, -u_time * 0.02)) - 0.5\",\n              \"  );\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float qx = q.x * u_scale * aspect;\",\n              \"  float qy = q.y * u_scale;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float tw = thread(qx, 0.09); // warp (vertical threads)\",\n              \"  float tf = thread(qy, 0.09); // weft (horizontal threads)\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  // Interlace: per cell, one direction sits over the other.\",\n              \"  float over = mod(floor(qx) + floor(qy), 2.0);\",\n              \"  float warpB = tw * (over < 0.5 ? 1.0 : 0.5);\",\n              \"  float weftB = tf * (over < 0.5 ? 0.5 : 1.0);\",\n              \"  float weave = max(warpB, weftB);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  // Sheen \\u2014 light travelling across a still cloth (this is the only motion).\",\n              \"  float sheen = fbm(q * 1.7 + vec2(u_time * 0.05, u_time * 0.028));\",\n              \"  weave *= 0.3 + 0.95 * sheen;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  // Fabric ground: near-black, faintly breathing between the shadow stops.\",\n              \"  vec3 base = mix(u_c0, u_c1, smoothstep(0.15, 0.8, sheen));\",\n              \"  base = mix(base, u_c2, smoothstep(0.62, 1.0, sheen) * 0.5);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  // Threads sit a touch above the ground.\",\n              \"  vec3 col = mix(base, u_c3, clamp(weave, 0.0, 1.0) * 0.55);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  // The accent runs through the threads \\u2014 a violet thread across the cloth.\",\n              \"  float amt = clamp(u_accentAmt, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"  col = mix(col, u_accent, amt * (0.08 + 0.34 * weave));\",\n              \"  col += u_accent * amt * 0.015;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  // A whisper of living grain, time-derived so it stays deterministic.\",\n              \"  col += (hash(gl_FragCoord.xy + floor(u_time * 9.0)) - 0.5) * 0.012;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  gl_FragColor = vec4(col, 1.0);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n\n            // The canvas is drawn at `resolution` × the frame size and stretched to fill it.\n            var width = Math.max(2, Math.round(root.clientWidth * resolution));\n            var height = Math.max(2, Math.round(root.clientHeight * resolution));\n            canvas.width = width;\n            canvas.height = height;\n            var gl = canvas.getContext(\"webgl2\", { alpha: false, premultipliedAlpha: true, antialias: false, depth: false, stencil: false, preserveDrawingBuffer: true });\n\n            function compile(type, source) {\n              var s = gl.createShader(type);\n              gl.shaderSource(s, source);\n              gl.compileShader(s);\n              if (!gl.getShaderParameter(s, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(s) || \"shader compile failed\");\n              return s;\n            }\n            function program(vertex, fragment) {\n              var p = gl.createProgram();\n              gl.attachShader(p, compile(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, vertex));\n              gl.attachShader(p, compile(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, fragment));\n              gl.linkProgram(p);\n              if (!gl.getProgramParameter(p, gl.LINK_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(p) || \"link failed\");\n              return p;\n            }\n            function texture(unit) {\n              var t = gl.createTexture();\n              gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n              gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, t);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_S, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_T, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n              return t;\n            }\n            // A texture the shader can render into.\n            function target(unit) {\n              var t = texture(unit);\n              gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA, width, height, 0, gl.RGBA, gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, null);\n              var f = gl.createFramebuffer();\n              gl.bindFramebuffer(gl.FRAMEBUFFER, f);\n              gl.framebufferTexture2D(gl.FRAMEBUFFER, gl.COLOR_ATTACHMENT0, gl.TEXTURE_2D, t, 0);\n              if (gl.checkFramebufferStatus(gl.FRAMEBUFFER) !== gl.FRAMEBUFFER_COMPLETE) throw new Error(\"incomplete framebuffer\");\n              gl.bindFramebuffer(gl.FRAMEBUFFER, null);\n              return { tex: t, fbo: f };\n            }\n            function bindTex(t, unit) {\n              gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n              gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, t);\n            }\n            var draw = function () {};\n            try {\n              if (!gl) throw new Error(\"WebGL2 is not available\");\n              var program_ = program(VERTEX, FRAGMENT);\n              gl.useProgram(program_);\n              var buffer = gl.createBuffer();\n              gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, buffer);\n              gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, new Float32Array([-1, -1, 3, -1, -1, 3]), gl.STATIC_DRAW);\n              var aPos = gl.getAttribLocation(program_, \"a_pos\");\n              gl.enableVertexAttribArray(aPos);\n              gl.vertexAttribPointer(aPos, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);\n              gl.viewport(0, 0, width, height);\n              function u(name) { return gl.getUniformLocation(program_, name); }\n              gl.uniform2f(u(\"u_res\"), width, height);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_scale\"), scale);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_warp\"), warp);\n              gl.uniform3f(u(\"u_c0\"), colors[0][0], colors[0][1], colors[0][2]);\n              gl.uniform3f(u(\"u_c1\"), colors[1][0], colors[1][1], colors[1][2]);\n              gl.uniform3f(u(\"u_c2\"), colors[2][0], colors[2][1], colors[2][2]);\n              gl.uniform3f(u(\"u_c3\"), colors[3][0], colors[3][1], colors[3][2]);\n              gl.uniform3f(u(\"u_accent\"), accent[0], accent[1], accent[2]);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_accentAmt\"), accentAmount);\n              var timeLoc = u(\"u_time\");\n              draw = function (frame) {\n                // remocn: u_time = (frame / fps) * speed\n                gl.uniform1f(timeLoc, (frame / 30) * speed);\n                gl.clearColor(0, 0, 0, 0);\n                gl.clear(gl.COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);\n                gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLES, 0, 3);\n              };\n            } catch (err) {\n              canvas.style.display = \"none\";\n              if (window.console) console.warn(\"shader-weave:\", err.message);\n            }\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"5\");\n            var totalFrames = Math.round(total * 30);\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(clock, {\n              frame: totalFrames,\n              duration: total,\n              ease: \"none\",\n              onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame); }\n            }, 0);\n            draw(0);\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"shader-weave\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
 "sha256": "6f18e97733eac5abf82f04bfdc769550f9d55c5201a7b0bd7f965b17b823d291",
